  "reason": "The strongest completed result is RNA-only multiprofile PCA with avgpool (accuracy 0.591, F1 0.573), clearly better than singleprofile PCA and multiprofile transformer aggregation, while image-only ResNet is much weaker. The main remaining uncertainty is whether a learned RNA representation can improve over PCA under the same already-promising profile and aggregation settings. config_005 changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200, isolating the representation effect while exploiting the best RNA-only direction. This is more informative than moving to multimodal fusion, which would change multiple factors at once and could confound whether any gain comes from the RNA encoder, image data, or fusion."
